WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
(white noise)

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:14.410
- My name is Mark Laita,
and I produce the videos

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:17.520
that you see on my channel,
Soft White Underbelly.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:20.060
I've been a photographer since I was 14.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:23.460
And I spent most of my career
doing advertising work.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:27.180
So I'm basically helping
wealthy corporations

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:28.280
become even wealthier.

00:00:29.131 --> 00:00:32.420
I realized as I got
older, that was my legacy.

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:34.560
And I didn't feel comfortable with that.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:37.920
So I wanted to do something
that mattered more in the world.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.280
The name Soft White Underbelly
came from Winston Churchill,

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.870
who back in World War II was
advising the United States

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:45.940
on how best to attack Germany.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:50.630
And he called Italy the
soft underbelly of Europe,

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:55.580
meaning that was the most
vulnerable spot that Germany had

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:56.680
to come in from Italy.

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:02.870
These videos are meant to
create awareness of things

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:04.420
that are broken in our country.

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:08.920
If we don't look at some of these things,

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.530
they're just gonna continue to grow

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:12.690
and get worse and worse.

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:17.240
And I believe listening,
understanding, accepting

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:20.280
and maybe deciding to
do something differently

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.058
might make a difference eventually,

00:01:22.058 --> 00:01:24.830
and help the next
generation or two of parents

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.273
raise kids who have more hope,

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:32.993
have better role models, have
both parents in their lives.

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:35.780
That's my hope.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:36.910
That's my aim with this work.

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:39.630
It's not to help the addict
that's outside my door,

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:40.510
even though I've done that.

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:41.510
I've done that many times.

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:45.650
Over the last 10 years, I've
talked with about 1,000 people

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:50.650
and financially I've probably
spent $150,000 helping people

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:54.980
with tents with, "Oh, you need shoes,

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:56.210
you need clothes, you need food,

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:58.530
you need a cell phone to
call your parole officer,

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:00.580
you need," all these kind of things.

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:02.670
Day after day after day,
every time I'm down here,

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:03.870
I'm bleeding money.

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:06.367
But that's not what this channel is about.

00:02:06.367 --> 00:02:07.850
It has nothing to do with this channel.

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:10.450
This channel is purely
about what I just said,

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:14.170
which is helping our society,
helping our government

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:17.440
figure out what's wrong with our country,

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:20.410
and hopefully build a better system.

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:22.617
Like the wealth inequality
that goes on here,

00:02:22.617 --> 00:02:26.940
the education and opportunity inequalities

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:29.450
create this stuff.

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:31.650
I mean, I talked to some of these kids,

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:33.440
or some of these people, and
said, "When they were kids,

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:36.730
they had no hope of a bright future.

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:38.820
There was no chance of it."

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:41.363
So that's what I think needs to change.

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:43.670
I've helped some addicts.

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:45.350
That's a personal thing I do.

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:47.660
It has nothing to do with this channel.

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:49.270
I'm just showing you some
things that are wrong

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:50.120
with the country.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:53.220
Sometimes that's just
too much to deal with.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:54.720
It's just too much to look at.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:59.520
And I'll watch these videos
or listen to these talks,

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:01.570
listen to these people, and I'll do it

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:03.520
on a more personal level,
a more like individual,

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:07.350
like I see self destructive
or self sabotaging behavior

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:11.160
in myself, and I'll be
able to apply the story

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:13.580
that I'm hearing, maybe not as extreme.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:15.553
Some of these stories
are really horrifying,

00:03:17.176 --> 00:03:19.400
and my childhood was nothing like these.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.830
But the mechanics are still the same.

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:23.190
You know, the stuff that happens to you

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:25.980
as a kid ends up affecting
the way you believe

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:29.860
in yourself, which ends
up manifesting as problems

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:36.440
with alcohol, or drugs, or your diet,

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:41.970
or taking care of your health,
or your choice of partners,

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:45.460
or your career choices,
or your belief in yourself

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:47.410
and the education that you decide to get.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:51.900
And there's so many things that
we're our own worst enemies

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:56.480
sometimes, and I think that's
an interesting story as well.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:57.727
And if you watch these
videos, you'll be like,

00:03:57.727 --> 00:04:00.550
"Wow, that's what was going on with them.

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:01.890
That's why they're doing
what they're doing."

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:04.100
And then you can kind of
apply it to your own life,

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:04.933
at least I can.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:10.180
Other times I just find
listening to all these talks

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:12.290
like a crash course in empathy.

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:14.107
I used to look at homeless people and go,

00:04:14.107 --> 00:04:15.820
"Man why don't they just get a job?

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:18.457
Quit the drug, get a job. Problem solved."

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:21.790
Now, after hearing all these stories,

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:23.150
I realize what these people have gone

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:24.980
through in their childhoods,
how they're broken,

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:26.170
how they never had a chance.

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:27.183
They never had hope.

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:34.570
And it's built my compassion
and empathy for these people,

00:04:35.132 --> 00:04:37.110
like nothing else.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:39.810
And then other times I can't
handle any of the above.

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:40.860
And I just watch these videos

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:42.860
as like interesting character studies.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:45.480
I get to listen to people
that I would never,

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:46.800
ever meet in my life.

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:49.360
And they're interesting and fascinating,

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:50.193
and I leave it at that.

00:04:50.193 --> 00:04:52.720
That's all I can bite off for the day.

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:55.710
So if you have the strength
and courage to watch

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:58.920
these videos, that's great.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:00.580
And if you don't, I understand.

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:01.880
They're not for everybody.

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:05.240
But if we're gonna change our country,

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:07.240
we're gonna need to
understand why it's broken,

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.660
what's wrong with it.

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:12.253
And here's a really good window
into what's really going on.

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:17.323
I hope you enjoy my work,
and thank you for watching.

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:23.410
Oh, and by the way, there's
a handful or more videos

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:27.083
that had been deleted from my
channel for various reasons.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:32.930
And starting tomorrow,
I'll start uploading

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:34.910
those videos again.

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:39.680
They're just slightly changed
to protect the subject

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:43.250
or for some reason just to meet YouTube's

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:44.610
community guidelines or whatever it takes

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.680
so that they don't get deleted.

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:49.273
And you'll start seeing those tomorrow.

00:05:49.273 --> 00:05:52.573
They're some of the best videos I've done,

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:55.150
and I just thought it was a
shame that they don't exist

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:55.983
on my channel.

00:05:55.983 --> 00:05:57.580
So you'll start seeing those tomorrow,

00:05:57.580 --> 00:05:59.370
and thank you for watching

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:03.350
(white noise)

